1
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,460
(Shen Teng)

2
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,060
(Bai Jingting)

3
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,260
(Jia Bing)

4
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:57,340
(Hu Xianxu)

5
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:01,820
(Wang Anyu)

6
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:04,100
(Fan Chengcheng)

7
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:06,340
(Huang Jingyu)

8
00:01:06,460 --> 00:01:08,380
(Wang Churan)

9
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:13,820
=Natural High S4=

10
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:32,340
(EP02 Part 2: Moo's here)

11
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:35,200
♪Say goodbye♪

12
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,640
♪Say goodbye♪

13
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,760
Have you heard Teng's new song?

14
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:46,220
(That voice is a 95% match!)

15
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:48,700
(Just vibing)

16
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:49,640
Can we get started already?

17
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:50,660
(Requesting a music cutoff)

18
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:53,880
(Bai Jingting)

19
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:56,280
You've already met the yaks.

20
00:01:58,480 --> 00:01:59,160
Yaks

21
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,640
(Black: natural coat, absorbs heat)
may look goofy,

22
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,680
(White: mutated, like lucky Tianzhu yaks)
but these guys

23
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,240
(Brown: cold-adapted, Spotted: yak-cow mix)
can run in -40°C

24
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:04,360
(Black: means strength in Zangzu culture)
without breaking a sweat.

25
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:06,520
(White: brings luck, guards plateau life)
Even in the thin air at 5,000 meters,

26
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:08,520
(Footage sourced online)
they haul loads like true plateau icons.

27
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:10,000
Yaks come in all kinds of colors.

28
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,720
Besides black, there's brown,

29
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:13,880
white, spotted, and more.

30
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:15,680
For your next challenge,

31
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:18,040
(Wang Anyu)
you'll be the plateau's ambassadors.

32
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:18,800
Pick a yak look

33
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,000
that suits your style.

34
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:25,900
(The ultimate yak headgear)

35
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:26,880
First come, first served.

36
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,120
I'm taking that one.

37
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:29,760
I want this one.

38
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,480
I'm going for a blond

39
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:32,080
mullet.

40
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,960
Toss me one.

41
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:35,860
(Coming right up)

42
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,300
(Quite the visual impact!)

43
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:57,520
Teng, wait a second.

44
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,600
You look just like Zhang Qiang.

45
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:58,960
I'm serious.

46
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:00,500
(The Zhang Qiang hairstyle)

47
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,560
Listen, darling.

48
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:06,720
I've basically got instant noodles

49
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,840
sitting on my head, right?

50
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:14,000
Use this as...

51
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,080
Yours looks cool. You've got highlights.

52
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:16,760
Anyu used to wear

53
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:18,400
his hair just like that.

54
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:20,280
(Serving looks!)

55
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:20,800
I already...

56
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:21,840
Hou Yi.

57
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:22,520
I've always had this...

58
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,160
Hou Yi?

59
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,280
You look like the Silver Horned King.

60
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:29,960
(Hair like the Silver Horned King's)
What if I call your name?

61
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,040
(Silver Horned King, Journey to the West)
Would you dare answer?

62
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,760
You look like you were born
with that hair.

63
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:35,720
(A little too perfect)

64
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:36,560
How did you...

65
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,560
How'd you pull that off?

66
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,440
You didn't even use a mirror,

67
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,200
and it fits you perfectly.

68
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,320
Jingyu picked a good one for me.

69
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:45,680
(The hairstylist is struggling)

70
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:46,240
This thing...

71
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,600
This thing's so itchy.

72
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,160
It's poking your eyes.

73
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,720
Wear the curly yellow one.

74
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:52,840
This curly one?

75
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:54,760
Mr. Huang.

76
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:55,560
It works.

77
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:56,520
(Yep, definitely Mr. Huang)

78
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:56,760
Okay, done.

79
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,960
Why do you keep

80
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,880
making finger hearts with your horns?

81
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,560
You two look exactly

82
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:06,680
like a pair of neighborhood gossips.

83
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:07,780
(The neighborhood gossip squad)

84
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:08,820
(Get a load of him!)

85
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:09,780
(Let me see!)

86
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:10,980
(Can you believe that?)

87
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:16,760
Bing!

88
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,320
(Fan Chengcheng)
Bing looks like... What's his name?

89
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,160
Fei Yangyang!

90
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,340
(Fei Yangyang's signature tan)

91
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:21,160
Mei Yangyang,

92
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:21,570
Xi Yangyang,

93
00:04:21,570 --> 00:04:22,980
and Fei Yangyang.

94
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,400
You look like the village chief,

95
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,880
but with a playful makeover.

96
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,160
You're more like Nuan Yangyang.

97
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,600
The one with the poop-shaped hair?

98
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:30,920
That's Lan Yangyang.

99
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,160
Wait, aren't we...

100
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,360
(Just checking)
Aren't we supposed to be cows?

101
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:37,660
(Quick! Cancel the sheep village!)

102
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,400
(Huang Jingyu)

103
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,160
Hu, that one's perfect for you.

104
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,700
(Give it a try)

105
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:47,340
(Let's see how it looks)

106
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:50,540
(Front-row fashion critique)

107
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,480
Get a feel for it.

108
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,840
(Hu Xianxu)

109
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,400
See? When you're the good-looking one,

110
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,080
you just hit different.

111
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,840
Now that's star power.

112
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:02,520
Seriously?

113
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:05,840
All these compliments

114
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:07,240
are about to go to my head.

115
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,720
Bet he'll still
be wearing that tomorrow.

116
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:11,760
Might as well get the full outfit.

117
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:15,720
Hi, everyone.

118
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:17,720
I thought the Natural High crew

119
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:19,040
had all turned into yaks.

120
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,600
Nope. We're yaks and Zhang Qiang.

121
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:23,740
(Jia Bing)

122
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:25,600
So how did these funny-looking yaks

123
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,840
(Chen Rui)
come to be?

124
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,440
They evolved from wild cattle.

125
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,360
(Footage sourced online)
Their close relatives include

126
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,400
(American bison)
American bison

127
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:32,160
and European bison.

128
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,280
(European bison)
When wild cattle reached the plateau,

129
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:33,840
they had to adapt

130
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:34,560
to life at high altitudes

131
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:35,560
and gradually evolved into yaks.

132
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:36,840
Along the way, they developed

133
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,320
some pretty amazing abilities.

134
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:40,000
Take their eyes,

135
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:40,960
their sense of smell,

136
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:41,680
and their hearing.

137
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:42,960
They all had to change.

138
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:43,960
And their vision?

139
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:44,880
They're farsighted.

140
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,400
They can see things far away,

141
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,880
but even distant objects

142
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,160
are just blurry outlines.

143
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,160
No wonder when I petted one earlier,

144
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:51,840
it totally ignored me.

145
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:53,080
I was too close for it to see, huh?

146
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:54,640
Sounds just like Teng.

147
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:55,880
Farsighted.

148
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:59,000
Too far to see clearly,
too close to see anything.

149
00:05:59,000 --> 00:05:59,800
(Neither near nor far works)

150
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,720
To give you a firsthand taste

151
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,680
of a yak's unusual vision,

152
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,040
your next challenge

153
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,440
will test your reflexes.

154
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:08,480
Let's see who can put on these goggles

155
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,600
and still track movement

156
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,520
like a yak.

157
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:12,560
Thank you, everyone.

158
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,760
This challenge is called

159
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:15,960
Dancing Yak.

160
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,800
First, one player is randomly chosen

161
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,120
to steal a seat.

162
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,760
(Dancing Yak)
That player picks a required dance move.

163
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,040
(Dancing Yak)
The seat-stealer taps

164
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,040
any seated player

165
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,240
on the shoulder.

166
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,080
The tapped player

167
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:26,720
must chase them using that dance move.

168
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,600
If the chaser catches them,

169
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:30,000
the seat-stealer must pick someone else.

170
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,920
If the chaser fails,

171
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:34,000
they become the next seat-stealer.

172
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,480
When time runs out,

173
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:37,640
whoever is still standing loses.

174
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:39,080
It's like Drop the Handkerchief.

175
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,760
I never played that.

176
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:44,040
You really guarded your stuff
as a kid, huh?

177
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,600
You never heard the song?

178
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:47,400
Oh, I know.

179
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:48,520
♪Drop, drop, drop the handkerchief♪

180
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:50,960
(Teaching the Gen Z kids)
♪Gently place it behind a little friend♪

181
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:52,080
Got it.

182
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:52,840
Let's go!

183
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:56,540
(Yak-vision goggles)

184
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:58,920
I can see you guys so clearly.

185
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:02,180
(Hu Xianxu's POV)

186
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:05,780
(Hu Xianxu's POV)

187
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:09,160
You scared me!

188
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,440
I thought you were way farther away.

189
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,080
Sorry!

190
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:17,860
(I didn't do anything!)

191
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,360
(My bad)

192
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:21,240
These things really mess
with your depth perception.

193
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,400
Hang on, mine are fogging up again.

194
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,840
It's the long johns making you sweat.

195
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,240
(Blame the long johns)
At least he skipped the winter hat today.

196
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:28,840
(No winter hat,)
But those leather pants...

197
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,260
(but rocking those leather pants)

198
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:30,700
(Annoyed! But where is everybody?)
Where are you?

199
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,360
Wait.

200
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,200
Wang Churan, is this

201
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,360
what you see every day?

202
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,520
Aren't you really nearsighted?

203
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:36,160
Yep. That's my vision
without contact lenses.

204
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:40,180
(Exactly like this)

205
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:47,100
(Hu Xianxu's POV)

206
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:48,160
Oh my God! This angle...

207
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,400
It's Zhang Qiang, the scientist.

208
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:52,820
(Zhang Qiang can pull off any look)

209
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:56,520
You scared me!

210
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:57,280
He scared me.

211
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,320
Let's do a practice round first

212
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,560
so everyone gets the hang of it.

213
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,120
Music, please.

214
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:06,100
(Dancing Yak: Practice Round)

215
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:07,160
Zhang Qiang!

216
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:17,040
Why are we one person short?

217
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:21,720
Isn't anyone sitting next to Churan?

218
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,760
Don't freak me out.

219
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,720
You mean we've had nine people
filming all morning?

220
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:34,920
This is getting ridiculous.

221
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:55,060
(Testing attack range)

222
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:03,100
(This is it!)

223
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:04,460
Time to strike.

224
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:06,820
(Still half a meter away)

225
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:16,060
(Who are you swinging at?)

226
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:18,840
Where's Wang Churan?

227
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:28,480
Why do I feel like
she should be right here?

228
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,280
This is terrifying.

229
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:43,060
(Failed again)

230
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:49,080
I can't lift my arms anymore.

231
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:51,400
My shoulders are killing me.

232
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:54,900
(Again)

233
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:57,500
(Failed again)

234
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:02,280
(Awkward chuckle)
Why am I so far off?

235
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:04,260
(Tap!)

236
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:04,980
(Instant counter-tap!)

237
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:07,420
(Deadlock!)

238
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:09,920
If you get caught,

239
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,280
you have to keep chasing

240
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,600
until you catch someone else.

241
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,040
That's the end of our practice round.

242
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:16,320
Everybody, got it?

243
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,840
With these goggles on,

244
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:18,800
everything looks really close,

245
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:19,640
but it's actually far away.

246
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:20,560
Exactly.

247
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,120
You can't reach them.

248
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:22,680
Now for the real thing.

249
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:23,800
(Dancing Yak: Game On!)

250
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:24,480
Let's go, Anyu.

251
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:25,440
I'll do it.

252
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,280
Time for your solo.

253
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:26,760
Yeah, solo time.

254
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,480
You guys take a breather.

255
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:29,440
Let me show you how it's done.

256
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:32,900
(Lead dancer)

257
00:10:34,220 --> 00:10:35,940
(General Wang prepares for his solo)

258
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,480
Don't make it too long.

259
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:40,000
Good call telling him that.

260
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:43,060
(Lead Dancer: Showtime!)

261
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:44,820
(Wang Anyu)

262
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:48,480
Let me come up with a move.

263
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:51,320
This one.

264
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:55,080
Just like that.

265
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:01,160
The second everyone sees Anyu's move,

266
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:02,280
their faces drop.

267
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:04,220
(Confirming the move)

268
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:06,100
(Searching for a target)

269
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:13,180
(Target acquired)

270
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:18,980
(Miss)

271
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:19,740
(Miss)

272
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:21,940
(Miss)

273
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,500
(Punching thin air)

274
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:29,220
(Gotcha!)

275
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,220
(The chase is on)

276
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:33,040
Get those hips moving.

277
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:36,660
(A little stiff)

278
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:41,220
(Super slow-mo)

279
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:44,180
(Turtle mode: slowly but surely)

280
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:49,900
(An elegant glance back)

281
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:51,420
