566
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:34,000
She's a goddess in heaven.

567
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,560
Heaven has a maternity ward too.

568
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:38,600
We can vote now.

569
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:39,580
(Not convinced)

570
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:41,560
Whenever the goddesses gave birth,

571
00:26:42,320 --> 00:26:44,320
their babies went to the nursery.

572
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:47,200
(Heaven)
A Yue was their postpartum nanny.

573
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:49,600
She helped them give birth and recover.

574
00:26:49,960 --> 00:26:50,680
But A Yue

575
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:51,960
mixed up the babies.

576
00:26:53,080 --> 00:26:55,160
(Fan Chengcheng? That's not my baby!)
It became a huge scandal.

577
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:56,480
Everyone in heaven

578
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:58,080
was talking about it.

579
00:26:58,560 --> 00:26:59,800
And that's how we got

580
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:02,340
"a yue hun zi".
[*A Yue mixed up the babies]

581
00:27:02,340 --> 00:27:03,940
(Fan Chengcheng's version
of "a yue hun zi": A heavenly baby mix-up)

582
00:27:04,580 --> 00:27:05,880
(Does that even make sense?)

583
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:08,480
I'm the only one with the real answer.

584
00:27:09,120 --> 00:27:10,760
It's not that complicated.

585
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:13,680
It's a blessing from an ethnic minority.

586
00:27:13,680 --> 00:27:15,720
(Hu Xianxu's version of "a yue hun zi":)
May you have

587
00:27:15,720 --> 00:27:18,000
(An ethnic minority blessing)
a healthy, chubby baby.

588
00:27:18,220 --> 00:27:20,280
(That actually makes sense)

589
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:22,400
Yours sounds a little more believable.

590
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:24,040
"A yue hun zi" is

591
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:25,400
a phrase

592
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:26,360
in ancient Persian.

593
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:30,280
Back to Once Upon
a Time in the Middle East again.

594
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:32,800
"A yue hun zi" is...

595
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:34,400
It's a nut.

596
00:27:34,780 --> 00:27:35,880
("A yue hun zi" is a nut)

597
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:36,880
Teng, you just

598
00:27:36,880 --> 00:27:38,400
made that up from what you're holding.

599
00:27:39,060 --> 00:27:40,980
(Inspired by whatever's in his hand)
Now it's called a pistachio.

600
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:42,080
How do you pronounce it?

601
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:44,440
"A yue hun zi".

602
00:27:47,860 --> 00:27:49,700
(Shen Teng's version of "A yue hun zi":
Ancient Persian for pistachio)

603
00:27:49,720 --> 00:27:51,360
Mine doesn't show the pronunciation.

604
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:52,360
I've been

605
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:53,480
wondering how to say it.

606
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:55,560
It's a secret password.

607
00:27:55,560 --> 00:27:57,840
(A password from a mythical tale)
It's from a story about the gods.

608
00:27:58,440 --> 00:27:59,760
Another story about gods?

609
00:27:59,760 --> 00:28:00,080
Yeah.

610
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,600
Lots of demons

611
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:02,120
and monsters

612
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:03,160
wanted

613
00:28:03,160 --> 00:28:03,880
to live forever.

614
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:06,520
You're copying Journey to the West!

615
00:28:08,760 --> 00:28:09,040
Yeah!

616
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:10,960
So they went
to the Queen Mother of the West

617
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:13,080
to eat her peaches of immortality.

618
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:16,120
(Queen Mother of the West)
You had to say the password to eat one.

619
00:28:17,020 --> 00:28:21,620
"A yue hun zi".

620
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:22,280
But

621
00:28:22,280 --> 00:28:23,240
nobody ever succeeded.

622
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:25,120
Because nobody knew

623
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,000
how to pronounce the spell.

624
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:27,200
"A yue hun zi"!

625
00:28:27,520 --> 00:28:29,160
Because "zi" is just a suffix.

626
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:30,680
So how do you say it?

627
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:34,160
"A yue hun".

628
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:37,760
So you swallow the "zi" a little?

629
00:28:39,520 --> 00:28:40,320
It's a suffix.

630
00:28:41,180 --> 00:28:42,240
(Wang Churan's version of "a yue hun zi":
A secret password from a mythical tale)

631
00:28:42,240 --> 00:28:43,160
Long ago,

632
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:44,960
there was a general

633
00:28:44,960 --> 00:28:45,800
who went to rescue a prince.

634
00:28:48,480 --> 00:28:49,800
To protect the prince,

635
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:51,640
he gathered all the village kids

636
00:28:51,640 --> 00:28:52,800
around the same age

637
00:28:53,120 --> 00:28:54,520
to disguise the prince.

638
00:28:55,160 --> 00:28:56,440
And the prince's name

639
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:57,400
was actually A Yue.

640
00:28:58,320 --> 00:28:59,440
It's an expression...

641
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:00,180
(A Yue)

642
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:01,720
From Jiangsu and Zhejiang.

643
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:02,560
They call it "a yue hun zi".
[*A Yue mixed in with the other kids]

644
00:29:03,820 --> 00:29:05,100
(Why's my hometown involved?)

645
00:29:06,800 --> 00:29:08,160
(Dead serious)
It's not pronounced in Mandarin.

646
00:29:08,560 --> 00:29:09,200
"A yue hun zi".

647
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:10,920
"A yue hun zi"?

648
00:29:11,640 --> 00:29:13,680
(Huang Jingyu's version of "a yue hun zi":)
It's actually a local legend.

649
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:14,160
(An old folk tale
from Jiangsu and Zhejiang)

650
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:15,800
Everyone mentioned "zi" earlier.

651
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:17,640
Some said prince or son.

652
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:19,080
But I'm telling you, "zi"

653
00:29:19,080 --> 00:29:20,000
means steamed buns.

654
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:21,720
The kind you eat.

655
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:23,160
"A yue"

656
00:29:23,800 --> 00:29:24,400
means

657
00:29:25,120 --> 00:29:25,800
this month.

658
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:28,480
So "a yue hun zi" means this month,

659
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:29,600
you only eat wontons and steamed buns.

660
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:38,120
What a great life that'd be!

661
00:29:38,120 --> 00:29:39,960
With meat and veggie fillings too!

662
00:29:39,960 --> 00:29:41,480
You're making fools of us!

663
00:29:41,540 --> 00:29:42,460
(Bai Jingting's version
of "a yue hun zi":)

664
00:29:42,460 --> 00:29:43,320
(Eating only wontons
and steamed buns for a month)

665
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:45,200
Get the Queen Mother and the wonton guy

666
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,080
out of here!

667
00:29:48,440 --> 00:29:49,760
I can't take those two anymore.

668
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:50,680
We all know they're bluffing,

669
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:52,080
but those two went way too far!

670
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:53,080
Get the Persian guy

671
00:29:53,080 --> 00:29:55,880
and the Jiangsu-Zhejiang guy out too!

672
00:29:55,880 --> 00:29:56,800
"A yue hun zi".

673
00:29:58,320 --> 00:29:59,000
What?

674
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:00,640
You're discriminating
against a dialect?

675
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:02,480
I think Wang Anyu might be right.

676
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:03,120
(Wang Anyu +1)

677
00:30:03,120 --> 00:30:03,960
Anyu's telling the truth.

678
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:05,060
(Wang Anyu +2)
Anyu's definitely right.

679
00:30:05,080 --> 00:30:06,480
I'm voting for Mr. Huang.

680
00:30:06,780 --> 00:30:07,840
(Huang Jingyu +1)

681
00:30:07,840 --> 00:30:09,920
The one with the real answer is...

682
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:15,520
Teng.

683
00:30:15,700 --> 00:30:16,920
(Shen Teng had the real answer)
It's a nut.

684
00:30:16,920 --> 00:30:18,280
Now it's called a pistachio.

685
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:20,800
Teng.

686
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:23,640
Pistachio!

687
00:30:23,820 --> 00:30:24,560
("A yue hun zi":
An old name for pistachio)

688
00:30:24,560 --> 00:30:25,200
A nut!

689
00:30:25,200 --> 00:30:25,710
(The name was recorded
in Li Xun's Tang-era Haiyao Bencao,)

690
00:30:25,710 --> 00:30:26,190
("a yue hun zi" comes from Persian.)

691
00:30:26,190 --> 00:30:26,750
(In the Yuan dynasty,
it was called "bi si da" or "hu zhen zi".)

692
00:30:26,750 --> 00:30:27,380
(Its cracked shell reveals
a green kernel, resembling a smile,)

693
00:30:27,390 --> 00:30:27,960
(so modern marketing
named it "kai xin guo".)

694
00:30:27,960 --> 00:30:29,840
Let's split into two teams again.

695
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:30,220
(Team lineup)

696
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:32,080
I'm worried about them.

697
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:34,120
All the big brains are on one team!

698
00:30:34,120 --> 00:30:34,500
(All "A")

699
00:30:34,500 --> 00:30:34,900
(The "Yue")

700
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:35,300
(Big "Hun")

701
00:30:35,300 --> 00:30:35,860
(Brains "Zi")

702
00:30:35,900 --> 00:30:37,100
(The ultimate brainpower team)

703
00:30:37,100 --> 00:30:38,140
(Each a genius in their own way)

704
00:30:38,140 --> 00:30:39,140
(Who's gonna challenge them?)

705
00:30:39,160 --> 00:30:39,720
No.

706
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:42,560
This game's all about confusing people.

707
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:43,280
When we're together,

708
00:30:43,280 --> 00:30:44,640
they won't know who's who.

709
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:45,480
And you think

710
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:47,440
Bai was actually trying earlier?

711
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:48,720
Actually.

712
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:50,160
That was just his warm-up.

713
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:51,240
He's hiding his true skills.

714
00:30:51,260 --> 00:30:53,780
(I'll take that as a compliment)

715
00:30:54,100 --> 00:30:55,300
=Natural High S4=

716
00:30:56,890 --> 00:30:59,680
Next up, it's four against four!

717
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:00,940
(Tall Tale King: official round)
In each round,

718
00:31:00,940 --> 00:31:02,720
(4 vs. 4 rules)
four players form the guessing team.

719
00:31:02,720 --> 00:31:04,640
Four others form the bluffing team.

720
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:05,400
Of those four,

721
00:31:05,400 --> 00:31:07,960
only one gets the real definition.

722
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:08,960
The other three

723
00:31:08,960 --> 00:31:10,240
have to make something up.

724
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,520
Once everyone's told their story,

725
00:31:11,520 --> 00:31:13,760
the guessing team gets just two guesses.

726
00:31:13,760 --> 00:31:14,720
If they guess wrong,

727
00:31:14,720 --> 00:31:15,800
they face a penalty.

728
00:31:15,800 --> 00:31:17,560
Or we could bring back

729
00:31:17,560 --> 00:31:19,160
that super addictive game.

730
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:22,240
Hand slapping.

731
00:31:23,100 --> 00:31:26,260
(Natural High Season 3, Episode 10)

732
00:31:27,360 --> 00:31:29,240
That deserves its own segment.

733
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:31,600
How about snapping a strap?

734
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:32,000
Sure.

735
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:33,770
(Losers get slapped on the arm)
Which team bluffs first?

736
00:31:33,800 --> 00:31:34,440
We'll go first.

737
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:35,040
Sure.

738
00:31:35,220 --> 00:31:37,040
(Guessing team, bluffing team)
Okay, we can go first.

739
00:31:37,040 --> 00:31:38,040
Hold your cards upright.

740
00:31:38,040 --> 00:31:40,040
You were all holding yours like this.

741
00:31:40,040 --> 00:31:41,600
But mine was written like this.

742
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:43,360
Let's go.

743
00:31:43,420 --> 00:31:44,095
(Guessing team, bluffing team)

744
00:31:44,095 --> 00:31:45,400
"Wang bu liu xing".
[*Cowherb seed, Chinese medicinal herb]

745
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:46,160
Hand out the cards.

746
00:31:48,620 --> 00:31:50,220
(Watching closely)

747
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,680
We can't share answers, right?

748
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:52,840
Whoever knows can't tell?

749
00:31:52,840 --> 00:31:54,200
Yeah. You can't tell each other.

750
00:31:54,200 --> 00:31:55,860
(Bluffing team can't share
the real definition)

751
00:32:00,320 --> 00:32:00,880
Jingyu, you're up.

752
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:05,400
"Wang bu liu xing".

753
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:07,860
(Hehehe)

754
00:32:08,020 --> 00:32:10,320
(Hehehe)

755
00:32:10,320 --> 00:32:11,000
I'm voting for Jingyu.

756
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:16,920
This story goes back

757
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:18,040
to a man named Wang Buliu.

758
00:32:18,040 --> 00:32:19,100
(Switching
to the Jiangsu-Zhejiang dialect)

759
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:22,480
There are actually
three more characters.

760
00:32:22,800 --> 00:32:23,520
"Wang bu liu xing"

761
00:32:23,520 --> 00:32:24,180
"feng dan ce".

762
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:25,640
You know...

763
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,920
"Feng" as in envelope.

764
00:32:27,920 --> 00:32:29,400
"Dan" as in pill.

765
00:32:29,400 --> 00:32:30,520
"Ce" as in handbook.

766
00:32:30,940 --> 00:32:32,520
("Wang bu liu xing, feng dan ce")

767
00:32:32,520 --> 00:32:33,600
It's from our
Jiangsu-Zhejiang dialect too.

768
00:32:33,600 --> 00:32:35,280
"Wang bu liu xing, feng dan ce"!

769
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:40,720
As for "wang bu liu xing"...

770
00:32:40,840 --> 00:32:41,760
It's about

771
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:42,680
a great General Wang.

772
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:45,080
Whenever he went to war,

773
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:47,040
the enemy couldn't track his movements.

774
00:32:47,320 --> 00:32:48,000
So they called him...

775
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:49,040
("Wang bu liu xing")
[*The untraceable General Wang]

776
00:32:49,040 --> 00:32:49,760
What does "feng dan ce"

777
00:32:49,760 --> 00:32:50,600
mean?

778
00:32:50,600 --> 00:32:51,440
(So professional)
I couldn't figure

779
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:52,160
that part out.

780
00:32:52,400 --> 00:32:53,640
What? Did they write your card

781
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:54,680
in the Jiangsu-Zhejiang dialect?

782
00:32:57,080 --> 00:32:57,560
Next!

783
00:32:58,500 --> 00:32:59,540
(Huang Jingyu's version
of "wang bu liu xing":)

784
00:32:59,540 --> 00:33:00,520
(An ancient general's military legend)

785
00:33:00,520 --> 00:33:02,720
What if this is his strategy?

786
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:04,600
Those three extra characters

787
00:33:04,600 --> 00:33:06,320
actually sound pretty good together.

788
00:33:07,100 --> 00:33:08,200
(A sincere smile)

789
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:09,040
"Wang bu liu xing"

790
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:10,160
is a medicinal herb.

791
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:13,440
Not even a king can stop its effects.

792
00:33:14,040 --> 00:33:15,160
That's why it's called "wang bu liu xing".
[*A king can't stop it]

793
00:33:16,320 --> 00:33:17,040
It improves blood circulation.

794
00:33:17,400 --> 00:33:18,600
It's extremely potent.

795
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:24,360
There are two other expressions

796
00:33:25,280 --> 00:33:25,800
that are similar.

797
00:33:26,120 --> 00:33:26,720
"Hua bu liu qiu".
[*Slippery as an eel]

798
00:33:28,520 --> 00:33:29,120
"Nian bu la ji".
[*All sticky and gooey]

799
00:33:29,380 --> 00:33:30,160
(Can someone stop him?)

800
00:33:30,160 --> 00:33:31,520
Slippery and sticky?

801
00:33:31,520 --> 00:33:32,560
Those don't mean the same thing.

802
00:33:32,840 --> 00:33:34,000
I didn't say they did!

803
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:35,160
They're just that kind of expression.

804
00:33:35,500 --> 00:33:36,020
All sticky and gooey.

805
00:33:36,020 --> 00:33:36,500
(Round and chubby)

806
00:33:36,500 --> 00:33:37,180
Slippery as an eel.

807
00:33:37,180 --> 00:33:37,500
(Dumb as a rock)

808
00:33:37,500 --> 00:33:38,340
Wang bu liu xing.

809
00:33:39,480 --> 00:33:41,640
Then why did
those two expressions survive?

810
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:42,620
(Explain that)

811
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:46,800
Because it never caught on!

812
00:33:46,820 --> 00:33:48,220
("Wang bu liu xing" doesn't catch on)
It didn't stick around.

813
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:49,920
Basically,

814
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:51,300
the emperor said,

815
00:33:51,300 --> 00:33:52,720
(Bai's version of "wang bu liu xing":)
"If it won't stay, so be it."

816
00:33:52,720 --> 00:33:54,280
(A medicinal herb that improves circulation)
That's how it improves circulation.

817
00:33:55,520 --> 00:33:56,120
Got it.

818
00:33:56,120 --> 00:33:57,240
This time, I'll tell you a story

819
00:33:57,240 --> 00:33:58,400
from the Classic of Mountains and Seas.

820
00:33:59,240 --> 00:34:00,560
Is the Queen Mother coming back?

821
00:34:00,580 --> 00:34:01,440
(Hooked on the story)

822
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:02,520
That's all I care about.

823
00:34:02,520 --> 00:34:03,560
The Queen Mother makes a cameo.

824
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,360
"Wang bu liu xing",

825
00:34:05,360 --> 00:34:07,600
originally,

826
00:34:07,600 --> 00:34:09,520
in the Classic of Mountains and Seas,

827
00:34:10,200 --> 00:34:12,040
there was a famous herb

828
00:34:12,040 --> 00:34:12,800
called "bu liu xing".

829
00:34:14,480 --> 00:34:16,640
Later, a doctor named Wang

830
00:34:16,640 --> 00:34:18,540
("Wang bu liu xing")

831
00:34:18,720 --> 00:34:20,880
saved many lives with this herb.

832
00:34:21,520 --> 00:34:22,600
So everyone started

