(A medicinal ingredient)
Slippery as an eel!

1362
00:51:23,200 --> 00:51:24,560
And sticky and gooey!

1363
00:51:25,440 --> 00:51:26,360
All slippery.

1364
00:51:27,120 --> 00:51:30,440
In ancient times, intestines
symbolized complicated thoughts.

1365
00:51:30,440 --> 00:51:32,480
If someone was simple-minded,

1366
00:51:32,480 --> 00:51:33,720
easygoing,

1367
00:51:34,360 --> 00:51:35,920
and kindhearted,

1368
00:51:35,920 --> 00:51:37,620
(Anyu's version of "wu chang gong zi":)
people called him that.

1369
00:51:37,620 --> 00:51:38,200
(An ancient term
for someone naive but kind)

1370
00:51:38,200 --> 00:51:39,400
So he's just naive.

1371
00:51:39,400 --> 00:51:39,960
Yeah.

1372
00:51:39,960 --> 00:51:40,920
But he's a good person.

1373
00:51:43,640 --> 00:51:45,880
Churan, tell us yours again.

1374
00:51:45,880 --> 00:51:46,800
It's an animal.

1375
00:51:48,200 --> 00:51:49,320
With no intestines.

1376
00:51:49,320 --> 00:51:50,080
Yeah.

1377
00:51:50,080 --> 00:51:50,920
Stop questioning her!

1378
00:51:50,920 --> 00:51:51,760
I'm picking you. Don't worry!

1379
00:51:52,360 --> 00:51:53,800
You just want her to get revenge!

1380
00:51:56,240 --> 00:51:56,680
Let's go!

1381
00:51:57,240 --> 00:51:57,960
Okay, sure.

1382
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:00,800
You're really picking me?

1383
00:52:03,980 --> 00:52:05,200
(The memories come flooding back)
How could you make me

1384
00:52:05,200 --> 00:52:06,240
hit a girl?

1385
00:52:12,640 --> 00:52:13,480
Got any water?

1386
00:52:13,640 --> 00:52:14,400
Wanna wet your hand?

1387
00:52:14,700 --> 00:52:16,040
(Of course)

1388
00:52:16,040 --> 00:52:16,800
Here, let's wet it.

1389
00:52:17,560 --> 00:52:18,320
You already wet yours.

1390
00:52:18,320 --> 00:52:19,440
Now I've gotta wet mine too?

1391
00:52:20,120 --> 00:52:22,200
When's this revenge cycle gonna end?

1392
00:52:22,200 --> 00:52:23,200
A little slap makes us friends. Come on.

1393
00:52:23,480 --> 00:52:23,840
Let's go.

1394
00:52:27,160 --> 00:52:28,480
It's a crab.

1395
00:52:28,480 --> 00:52:29,440
People thought it had no intestines.

1396
00:52:29,440 --> 00:52:31,320
But that was a misconception.

1397
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:35,520
Wait.

1398
00:52:40,080 --> 00:52:40,320
Three!

1399
00:52:49,540 --> 00:52:54,620
(A stylish guy
over 40 doing his daily skincare)

1400
00:52:55,480 --> 00:52:55,720
Two!

1401
00:53:01,320 --> 00:53:02,320
How could you make me

1402
00:53:02,320 --> 00:53:03,400
hit a girl?

1403
00:53:03,720 --> 00:53:04,000
One!

1404
00:53:04,800 --> 00:53:05,200
I'm running!

1405
00:53:06,400 --> 00:53:07,200
I'm running!

1406
00:53:07,200 --> 00:53:08,460
(Correct guess)

1407
00:53:08,680 --> 00:53:09,480
I'm running!

1408
00:53:12,760 --> 00:53:13,600
It really was you?

1409
00:53:16,040 --> 00:53:17,120
It really is her!

1410
00:53:22,440 --> 00:53:23,600
No choice now. Come on!

1411
00:53:29,800 --> 00:53:30,200
Have a seat.

1412
00:53:30,200 --> 00:53:31,200
It really was her!

1413
00:53:33,800 --> 00:53:34,920
Wet my hand too!

1414
00:53:41,120 --> 00:53:42,560
You think us women
are scared of this? Come on.

1415
00:53:47,640 --> 00:53:48,040
Three!

1416
00:53:49,480 --> 00:53:49,880
Two!

1417
00:53:57,560 --> 00:53:57,880
One!

1418
00:54:02,080 --> 00:54:02,720
I went easy.

1419
00:54:02,720 --> 00:54:03,500
(Now he's being a gentleman)

1420
00:54:04,220 --> 00:54:05,460
(What a shame)

1421
00:54:09,160 --> 00:54:09,600
That hurt.

1422
00:54:09,760 --> 00:54:10,480
Do it again.

1423
00:54:10,480 --> 00:54:11,160
No, it hurts.

1424
00:54:11,680 --> 00:54:13,600
You've grown up.

1425
00:54:13,920 --> 00:54:15,760
He really wanted her to get revenge.

1426
00:54:15,760 --> 00:54:16,520
To get him back.

1427
00:54:16,520 --> 00:54:17,680
Yeah, he wanted her to get revenge.

1428
00:54:17,680 --> 00:54:19,200
Didn't expect another correct guess.

1429
00:54:20,960 --> 00:54:22,480
His heart was in the right place.

1430
00:54:22,640 --> 00:54:25,280
She made such a big show of it too.

1431
00:54:25,280 --> 00:54:26,920
Getting water and everything.

1432
00:54:27,400 --> 00:54:29,520
So what's the actual meaning?

1433
00:54:29,520 --> 00:54:31,380
(Curious Bai is back)

1434
00:54:31,540 --> 00:54:32,220
("Wu chang gong zi": Modern biology confirms
crabs have intestines,)

1435
00:54:32,220 --> 00:54:32,960
(but ancient people knew little about anatomy
and mistakenly thought they had none,)

1436
00:54:32,960 --> 00:54:33,618
(and jokingly called them "gentlemen")
It's a crab.

1437
00:54:33,618 --> 00:54:34,080
(for walking sideways.)
It's a crab.

1438
00:54:34,080 --> 00:54:34,849
(Hence the elegant nickname)
What's such

1439
00:54:34,849 --> 00:54:35,480
("wu chang gong zi".)
What's such

1440
00:54:35,480 --> 00:54:36,680
a fancy name supposed to describe?

1441
00:54:36,680 --> 00:54:39,360
Some guy selling pig organs
in Jiangsu and Zhejiang?

1442
00:54:40,160 --> 00:54:41,680
The offal seller was the worst one.

1443
00:54:41,680 --> 00:54:42,320
An offal seller!

1444
00:54:43,400 --> 00:54:44,280
Last question.

1445
00:54:44,700 --> 00:54:46,800
("He hua da shao",
bluffing team, guessing team)

1446
00:54:46,800 --> 00:54:48,000
"He hua da shao"?

1447
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:48,880
("He hua da shao")

1448
00:54:48,880 --> 00:54:50,640
"He hua da shao" means

1449
00:54:50,640 --> 00:54:51,720
a playboy.

1450
00:54:52,760 --> 00:54:53,680
Basically,

1451
00:54:55,520 --> 00:54:57,120
a rich, handsome guy from back then.

1452
00:54:58,680 --> 00:55:00,320
Dressed in fancy clothes,

1453
00:55:01,040 --> 00:55:02,000
loved admiring flowers.

1454
00:55:03,160 --> 00:55:04,760
(Breaking news)
It's often used to describe

1455
00:55:05,180 --> 00:55:07,180
someone who looks amazing

1456
00:55:07,180 --> 00:55:09,460
but has nothing upstairs.

1457
00:55:09,700 --> 00:55:10,300
(Fan Chengcheng's version
of "he hua da shao":)

1458
00:55:10,300 --> 00:55:10,960
(Someone who's good-looking
but empty-headed)

1459
00:55:10,960 --> 00:55:13,640
Mine is complete opposite
of Chengcheng's story.

1460
00:55:14,760 --> 00:55:17,320
He hung around

1461
00:55:17,320 --> 00:55:18,640
a group of spoiled rich boys.

1462
00:55:18,640 --> 00:55:19,400
But

1463
00:55:19,400 --> 00:55:20,320
he stayed pure despite it all.

1464
00:55:20,720 --> 00:55:22,040
He was a real person.

1465
00:55:22,400 --> 00:55:23,720
A warlord

1466
00:55:23,720 --> 00:55:24,960
who loved writing poetry.

1467
00:55:24,960 --> 00:55:26,240
But I can't remember

1468
00:55:26,240 --> 00:55:27,200
the exact poem.

1469
00:55:27,200 --> 00:55:28,800
He wrote a silly little rhyme.

1470
00:55:29,940 --> 00:55:31,370
Daming Lake is really wide,

1471
00:55:31,370 --> 00:55:33,310
Lotus flowers bloom inside,

1472
00:55:33,310 --> 00:55:34,940
Toads sit on them with pride.

1473
00:55:34,940 --> 00:55:36,080
Poke it, and watch it flee!

1474
00:55:36,080 --> 00:55:38,320
So people nicknamed him "he hua da shao".
[*Lotus young master]

1475
00:55:38,960 --> 00:55:40,400
(Hu Xianxu's version of "he hua da shao":)
Later, it became a compliment.

1476
00:55:40,400 --> 00:55:41,026
(Praising someone)
Who'd you go out with? Young Master Hua.

1477
00:55:41,026 --> 00:55:41,880
(who stays pure despite bad influences)
Who'd you go out with? Young Master Hua.

1478
00:55:42,840 --> 00:55:43,440
Who's that beside him?

1479
00:55:43,440 --> 00:55:44,280
It's Lady Hua!

1480
00:55:46,920 --> 00:55:48,680
One explanation is that

1481
00:55:48,680 --> 00:55:50,600
"da" and "tai" mean the same thing.
[*Big and Too]

1482
00:55:50,600 --> 00:55:53,040
("Da" = "Tai")
So "da shao" means "too few".

1483
00:55:53,040 --> 00:55:54,080
("Da shao" = too few)
They're interchangeable characters.

1484
00:55:54,080 --> 00:55:55,240
Another explanation

1485
00:55:55,240 --> 00:55:56,280
comes from the Book of Guiguzi.

1486
00:55:56,920 --> 00:55:59,000
You can't have it all.

1487
00:55:59,000 --> 00:56:01,680
Whether you like peach blossoms,

1488
00:56:01,680 --> 00:56:03,280
lotuses, or apricot blossoms,

1489
00:56:03,280 --> 00:56:05,040
whatever your favorite is,

1490
00:56:05,360 --> 00:56:06,440
the bigger the lotus,

1491
00:56:06,440 --> 00:56:07,360
(Lotus)
the fewer there are.

1492
00:56:07,360 --> 00:56:08,720
Smaller peach blossoms

1493
00:56:08,720 --> 00:56:09,480
come in greater numbers.

1494
00:56:11,240 --> 00:56:12,520
You want them beautiful

1495
00:56:12,520 --> 00:56:13,440
and big.

1496
00:56:14,560 --> 00:56:16,040
But if they're big,

1497
00:56:16,040 --> 00:56:16,920
there are fewer!

1498
00:56:21,600 --> 00:56:24,000
Big lotus flowers are rare!

1499
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:24,920
Fewer big ones!

1500
00:56:25,440 --> 00:56:26,880
(Shen Teng's version of "he hua da shao":)
Guiguzi sure had time to kill!

1501
00:56:26,880 --> 00:56:28,240
(You can't have everything)
He even wrote that down?

1502
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:32,800
The big ones really are rare!

1503
00:56:33,760 --> 00:56:35,680
He's cracking himself up!

1504
00:56:37,580 --> 00:56:39,520
Next!

1505
00:56:39,520 --> 00:56:40,520
"He hua da shao".

1506
00:56:42,960 --> 00:56:45,000
It's actually a deity people worship.

1507
00:56:45,480 --> 00:56:46,920
It's a folk legend.

1508
00:56:47,040 --> 00:56:48,640
People harvest lotus roots
from ponds, right?

1509
00:56:48,640 --> 00:56:50,620
People used to make a living doing that.

1510
00:56:51,520 --> 00:56:52,790
Strong men would go in,

1511
00:56:53,960 --> 00:56:55,880
but some never came back.

1512
00:56:56,800 --> 00:56:59,040
When someone fell in, they'd...

1513
00:57:00,200 --> 00:57:01,720
You know how you instinctively

1514
00:57:01,720 --> 00:57:02,880
grab something when you fall?

1515
00:57:03,200 --> 00:57:05,360
They'd pull all the big lotuses down!

1516
00:57:06,040 --> 00:57:07,640
So the bigger lotuses

1517
00:57:07,640 --> 00:57:09,120
became fewer and fewer.

1518
00:57:09,120 --> 00:57:10,760
They dragged them all underwater!

1519
00:57:13,160 --> 00:57:14,040
Every single one!

1520
00:57:17,360 --> 00:57:18,120
And then,

1521
00:57:18,520 --> 00:57:20,480
there was this young master

1522
00:57:20,480 --> 00:57:22,040
from a village near the lotus pond.

1523
00:57:23,600 --> 00:57:24,560
He was very kind.

1524
00:57:24,560 --> 00:57:25,520
He spent some money

1525
00:57:25,520 --> 00:57:26,360
on safety measures.

1526
00:57:27,040 --> 00:57:27,720
But who would've thought?

1527
00:57:27,720 --> 00:57:28,840
He fell in too.

1528
00:57:29,000 --> 00:57:30,200
So they worshipped him

1529
00:57:30,200 --> 00:57:31,480
(Jia Bing's version of "he hua da shao":)
and gave him that name.

1530
00:57:31,480 --> 00:57:32,900
(A kindhearted man who helped others)

1531
00:57:35,000 --> 00:57:36,280
I still think it's Chengcheng.

1532
00:57:36,760 --> 00:57:37,520
Then step into the ring.

1533
00:57:38,520 --> 00:57:38,960
Into the ring!

1534
00:57:41,200 --> 00:57:41,640
Into the ring!

1535
00:57:42,720 --> 00:57:43,160
Into the ring!

1536
00:57:43,160 --> 00:57:44,940
(Fated showdown: Round three)

1537
00:57:48,440 --> 00:57:49,560
Churan picks Chengcheng.

1538
00:57:53,460 --> 00:57:55,420
(Will the third time
finally bring revenge?)

1539
00:57:55,540 --> 00:57:57,200
(Everyone's enjoying the show)

1540
00:57:57,200 --> 00:57:57,960
Can't wait.

1541
00:57:58,280 --> 00:58:00,600
I've been looking forward to this.

1542
00:58:01,390 --> 00:58:02,280
I've been waiting

1543
00:58:02,560 --> 00:58:03,400
